rustls-ffi-quic (0.15.7+quic3-1~smallgearlab1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The QUIC API follows the conventions of rustls-ffi (rustls_result for what
    can fail, getters named get_*): _get_alert, _get_secret,
    _get_negotiated_ciphersuite, _get_peer_certificate (a rustls_certificate,
    then rustls_certificate_get_der) and _get_peer_transport_parameters replace
    the functions that returned a bool. The helper before 1.16.0-1~smallgearlab3
    does not work with it: Breaks, and dh_makeshlibs -V names this version.
  * rustls_quic_connection_write_hs kept nothing of what did not fit in the
    caller's buffer; it keeps it now.

