rustls-ffi-quic (0.15.7+quic2-1~smallgearlab1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * From the tag v0.15.7+quic2 (on the branch renamed): the new function
    rustlsq_quic_connection_peer_certificate returns the certificates that the
    server sent over a QUIC connection, which curl needs to check a pinned
    public key over HTTP/3. The soname is the same, so the dependency of the
    packages that use it names the version (dh_makeshlibs -V).
  * main (upstream's names) and renamed (the renaming as one commit) are two
    branches now; the package is built from a tag on renamed.

